Events reported through registry data provide us with a platform to investigate further by initially informing us of the event, which we will then follow up in primary and secondary care records to collect highly relevant outcome data such as cancer grade, size and receptor status. This information informs our secondary and exploratory objectives which are breast cancer and all-cause mortality, cancers other than breast, cardiovascular/cerebrovascular events, and fractures.

